1 NAME Xiē /HUANG 黄歇 73A/
2 GIVN Xiē
2 _MARNM HUANG 黄歇 73A
1 NAME HUANG Xie, 黄歇 73A
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE -238
1 BIRT
2 DATE -314
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 73rd generation. 314 BC to 238 BC. Son of Zong Bo (宗伯). From Huang Guo (黄国), present day Huang Chuan County in Henan (河南潢川县). Also known as Lord Chun Shen (春申君).
2 CONT
2 CONT Nobleman (公子), Prince's Tutor (太傅), General (春申君) and Prime Minister (令尹) of the State of Chu (楚国) during the Warring States (战国) period. One of the Four Lords of the Warring States (战国四公子). He had more than 3,000 followers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Xie was assassinated by his brother-in-law, Li Yuan (李园), in 238 BC when Emperor Chu Kao Lie (楚考烈) died. His residence was sacked and his family members there were massacred. Fortunately, his 3rd son, You Chong (幼冲), also known as
2 CONC  Tang (堂), was away in the Wu (吴) district and therefore escaped death. According to another internet source, Douban (豆瓣), his youngest son, Jiu (究), sensed and avoided the massacre with the help of some of Huang Xie's followers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a total of 13 sons - Shang (尚), Jun (俊), Tang (堂, or Yong, 咏), Xiang (珦), Hui (晖), Shao (韶), Wang (往), Qing (擎), Ping (平), Xi (曦), An (安), Shu (述) and Jiu (究) - by 2 wives - Madam Li (李氏) and Madam Ji (姬氏).
2 CONT
2 CONT Xie (歇) was credited with building hydrological works on the "three rivers of Wu" - East River, Lou River and Wusong River - that helped to prevent floods and develop agriculture. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Shanghai's Huangpu River was named after the surname "Huang" (黄) of Lord Chun Shen. The city is also called Shen Chen (申城), or City of Shen, in honour of Lord Chun Shen. In 2002, the Shanghai government rebuilt the Temple of Lord 
2 CONC Chun Shen on the site of the ancient Temple in Chun Shen Village. Lord Chun Shen's tomb is said to be located in Huainan (淮南市), Anhui (安徽) province, 12 kilometres outside of Shouchun (寿春). The tomb measures 90 metres by 80 metres 
2 CONC and is 11 metres high.
2 CONT
2 CONT His grave was also spotted at the Huang Mausoleum (黄国故城), in Huangchuan (潢川), Henan (河南) on 7 October 2024. It was located in an area within the Mausoleum designated as the Chunshen Cemetery (春申陵园).
2 CONT
2 CONT 七十三世。公元前314 - 公元前238。宗伯之子, 幼冲 (堂) 之父。楚国江夏人, 源籍楚国属国黄国 (今河南省潢川县)。战国时期楚国大臣, 是着名的政治家。与魏国信陵君魏无忌, 赵国平原君赵胜, 齐国孟尝君田文并称为“战国四公子”, 曾任楚相。黄歇游学博文, 善辩。楚考烈王元年 (公元前262) 以黄歇为相, 封为春申君, 赐淮北地12县。
2 CONT
2 CONT 公元前238年, 楚考烈王病逝, 春申君在前去奔丧, 李园令人埋伏于棘门之内, 杀死春申君及全家。巧幸春申君的三子幼冲 (堂) 当时身在吴地而逃过劫数。跟据豆瓣的记载黄歇的第十三子(究)事先知其劫难, 在众多门客保护下逃离免遭被杀。
2 CONT
2 CONT 上海简称“申”也是源自受封于这里的春申君黄歇。黄歇未封吴地之时, 黄浦江也不叫黄浦江, 而且这条河由于泥沙淤积, 河床过高, 一到汛期常常洪水泛滥, 老百姓苦不堪言。黄歇到后, 就对这条河进行治理, 疏通了河道, 筑起了提垻, 使这条河不在泛滥, 造福了当地的百姓。人们为了怀念他, 将这条河改称为春申江或黄浦江, 简称申江。后来, “申”字就成了上海的代称。
2 CONT
2 CONT 黄歇疏通河道, 抑制水患, 政绩显赫, 深得民心。当地人纷纷以其姓或号为许多山, 水, 地方命名, 如浙江吴兴的黄埔, 江苏江阴的申港, 黄田港, 江苏江阴的君山也叫黄山。在上海, 黄浦江, 申江, 春申江, 黄浦区, 黄申路, 春申村等, 均为纪念这位开申之祖。    
2 CONT
2 CONT NB -  In an internet article published by 联合新闻网 titled 黄姓起源有三 on 24 April 2019, it was mentioned that  Tang (堂) was the 5th son. For the purpose of my Family Tree here, I have used the information from 黄守恭 - 百度百科.
2 CONT
