1 NAME Chén Hú 陳瑚, 115, 74, 27,11世
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hu[1] was an official during the Jianlong[2] era. On his plan to subjugate Jingnan[3], he did not use the one put forth by Yu[4]. Instead, he bestowed gifts on Chancellor You[5], who proposed the Han6 scheme. This 
2 CONC plan failed and he was demoted and sent to Longxi[7],  Fujian[]8.  Hu had thirteen sons. The first four were Han, Long, Lie and Yi[9] .  Han, Long, and Yi formed a Social Alliance in Dongxubing[10] to support  Shi Zong[11], Ren Zo
2 CONC ng[12], and Jia You[13] because they were upright officials. Lie[14] secretly went to Fuzhou[15] , where he was appointed a position, even though he was a commoner, to the Imperial College[16]. His lectures were not appreciated by
2 CONC  his students. Together with his cousins he traveled to Jinzhou[17]. Lie had one son, named Gui[18].
2 CONT
2 CONT ~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Hu (Chinese: 瑚; pinyin: Hú; Hoisanva: Vũ)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Jianlong ([960 - 963 C.E.];  Chinese: 建隆; pinyin: Jiànlóng; Hoisanva: Gèin Lung) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Jingnan (Chinese: 荊南; pinyin: Jīngnán; Hoisanva: Gëin Nãm)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Yu (Chinese: 虞; pinyin: Yú; Hoisanva: Nguĩ)
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 You (Chinese: 尤; pinyin: Yóu; Hoisinva: Yiũ)
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 Han (traditional Chinese: 韓; simplified Chinese: 韩; pinyin: Hán; Hoisanva: Hõn)
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 Longxi (traditional Chinese: 龍溪; simplified Chinese: 龙溪; pinyin: Lóngxī; Hoisanva: Lũng Käi)
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 Fujian (a province in south China; Chinese: 福建; pinyin: Fújiàn; Hoisanva: Fūk Gèin)
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 Han, Long, Lie and Yi (traditional Chinese: 漢隆烈繹; simplified Chinese: 汉隆烈绎; pinyin: Hàn, Lóng, Liè, and Yì; Hoisanva: Hön, Lũng, Lèik, and Yèik).
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 Dongxubing (traditional Chinese: 東旭炳; simplified Chinese: 东旭炳; pinyin: Dōngxùbǐng; Hoisanva: Üng Gūk Bēin)
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Shi Zong (Chinese: 仕宗; pinyin:  Shì Zōng; Hoisanva: Xù Düng)
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 Ren Zong (Chinese: 仁宗; pinyin: Rén Zōng; Hoisanva: Ngĩn Düng)
2 CONT
2 CONT 13 Jia You(Chinese: 嘉佑; pinyin: Jiā Yòu; Hoisanva: Gä Yiù)
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 Lie (Chinese: 烈; pinyin: Liè; Hoisanva: Lèik)
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 Fuzhou (Chinese: 福州; pinyin: Fúzhōu; Hoisanva: Fūk Jiü)
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 Imperial College (The Imperial college was the highest institute in Imperial China; traditional Chinese: 國字監; simplified Chinese: 国字监; pinyin: Guózìjiān; Hoisanva: Gōk Dù Gäm)
2 CONT
2 CONT 17 Jinzhou (Chinese: 金州; pinyin: Jīnzhōu; Hoisanva: Gïm Jiü)
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 Gui (Chinese: 圭; pinyin: Guī; Hoisanva: Gï).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sites.fitnyc.edu/users/gene_chin/tree/000-0080qian.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 阳春春城陈氏族谱（谟祖） http://bbs.chens.org.cn/fengtai/show.aspx?&id=563&cid=15
2 CONT
2 CONT 瑚公下傳十九世綜合世系圖 http://www.nanchens.com/csyy/csyy03/csyy03007.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 陈凤台世系研究：福建龙溪世系（由陈瑚至陈文） http://bbs.chens.org.cn/fengtai/show.aspx?id=443&cid=13
2 CONT
2 CONT 依据广东「陈凤台七子」的族谱，「吾祖陈瑚」是公认存在的。只是，有关他的生平记载，一则正史上找不到，二是年代上不相符。因此现时争议不少。但是若据阳江润祖（陈凤台第五子）族谱，除了把他称「陈湖，字汉臣」之外，还有向上连接世系，竟然一直至陈洪进，这是我在网上能读到的唯一如此有名有号版本。因此，姑且采用，以后有新发现才作更正。暂且把他列为「陈洪进第5代孙」吧。
