2 CONT * Cao Daoheng and Shen Yucheng, Zhonggu wenshi ziliao congkao, 149–51. 
2 CONT * Goodman, Howard L. “A History of Court Lyrics in China during Wei-Chin Times.” Asia Major 19.1–2 (2006): 57–109. 
2 CONT * Goodman, Howard L. “Tintinnabulation of Bells: Scoring Prosody in Third-Century China and Its Relationship to Yüeh-fu Party Music.” Journal of the American Oriental Society 126.1 (2006): 27–49. 
2 CONT * Wang Fuli 王福利. Jiaomiao yanshe geci yanjiu 郊廟燕射歌辭研究, 212–16. Beijing: Xueyuan chubanshe, 2009. 
2 CONT * Goodman, Howard L. “Sites of Recognition: Burial, Mourning, and Commemoration in the Xun Family of Yingchuan.” Early Medieval China 15 (2009): 49–90. 
2 CONT * Goodman, Howard L. Xun Xu and the Politics of Precision in Third-Century AD China. Leiden: E. J. Brill, 2010.
