2 CONC Xiang(3) [7005], Zheng(1) Mu [7187], and Chen(1) Lie [3076] were called the 'Four Teachers' (si xiansheng) and were extremely close. Xiang(3) was buried in Changzhou, Yixing xian. Fu(5) Ji's[7225] and Fang(1) Meng's [7220] father-
2 CONC in-law, Zheng(1) Mu's [7187] and Liu(2) Yi(1)'s [1201] brother-in-law (his sisters' husbands). Xu(3) Chang's [742] friend. Several grandsons moved to Suzhou, Changshu xian from Changzhou, Yixing xian. His descendant Zun [7131] mar
2 CONC ried a daughter of Li(2) Heng [7276] and moved to Suzhou, Kunshan xian. Chen(1) Bozhen [3078], an eighth generation descendant of the branch of the family that remained in Fujian and lived in Fuzhou, Changlo xian, was Guangdong yu
